:: WednesdayCircle {"title":"Chapter II / A More Useful Theory","scene":"kitchen"}
# A more useful theory

@Chapter("CHAPTER II · WEEK THREE", "The group gets practical")

Your weekly empowerment circle has one guest and twelve empty chairs. You guide a
breathing exercise about taking up space under systems built to make women smaller.

::: dialogue {.dialogue speaker="Mars" mood="helpful"}
“The system making me smallest is my bank balance.”
:::

The guest opens her eyes. “She has a point.”

The next week, six people come. You explain structures. Mars knows their street
addresses, bail schedules, unreliable exes, and which engine noise means **do not
drive this car to work tomorrow**.

After the last guest leaves, Mars says you need people to be broken so you can be
the least broken person in the room.

You tell her Cal keeps towing her life away because she hands him the keys.

The argument stops one inch before becoming honest.

[[Kiss her and call it mutual aid -> Kiss]]

[[Apologize without explaining the apology -> Apology]]

[[Win the argument; sleep alone -> WinArgument]]

:: Kiss {"title":"Chapter II / Mutual Aid","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $trust += 2
@do $leverage += 1
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Their first kiss ended an argument without resolving it."})

@Chapter("INCIDENT REPORT", "Mutual aid")

You kiss her. Mars holds your wrist as if checking whether you can still leave.

“This does not define us,” you say afterward.

“Say mutual aid and I am going back to Cal.”

You kiss her again.

[[Three weeks later, a profitable complaint arrives -> FirstTow]]

:: Apology {"title":"Chapter II / No Framework","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $trust += 3
@do $honesty += 2
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora apologized once without naming a social structure."})

@Chapter("INCIDENT REPORT", "No framework")

“That was cruel,” you say. “And it was about me, not Cal.”

Mars studies you, suspicious of a sentence with no framework attached.

She kisses your cheek on the way to bed. It is gentler than either of you knows how
to discuss.

[[Three weeks later, a profitable complaint arrives -> FirstTow]]

:: WinArgument {"title":"Chapter II / Technically Correct","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $trust -= 2
@do $leverage += 2
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora won an argument and spent the night listening for Mars to leave."})

@Chapter("INCIDENT REPORT", "Technically correct")

You prove every point. Mars runs out of jokes. She sleeps in the spare room while
you listen to the secondhand air conditioner cough dust through the wall.

In the morning she is still there. You count this as victory.

[[Three weeks later, a profitable complaint arrives -> FirstTow]]

